    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220-a3">

                <pb facs="0382" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg288"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 667.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                        1896.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The secretary of state for foreign affairs presents his compliments to Mr. Bayard
                    and begs to acknowledge the receipt of his note of the 18th instant on the
                    subject of the Bering Sea award.</p>
                <p>The secretary of state for foreign affairs has the honor to acquaint Mr. Bayard,
                    in reply, that the matter has been referred to the proper department of Her
                    Majesty’s Government.</p>
            </div>
